// x-engine-firing-07: the restart builtins (count, once, take, skip, uniq,
// hold) clear their latch in sleep() but keep their output, so a re-selected
// arm whose input does not fire at the wake emits the previous activation's
// value, and a restarted builtin is not a fresh one.
//
// command: graphix-fuzz run design/review-2026-10-05/repro/x-engine-firing-07.gx
//
// Arm 1 counts in1 twice (1, 2). in0=2 selects arm 2, whose count is fresh;
// in0=1 re-selects arm 1, whose count restarted at 0 in sleep(). in1's fires
// were consumed while arm 1 was awake, so at both wakes count's input
// arrives STALE and nothing counts.
//
// expected: a restarted count behaves as arm 2's fresh count does at epoch 3,
// nothing (then 1):
//   Trace([0:i64:-1]; [0:i64:1]; [0:i64:2]; []; []; [0:i64:1])
// (under pause it would be 2 and then 3; it is never 2 and then 1)
// observed, every mode (interp, jit, no cache, cold, warm; `check` says AGREE):
//   Trace([0:i64:-1]; [0:i64:1]; [0:i64:2]; []; [0:i64:2]; [0:i64:1])
// the wake shows the pre-restart 2, and the next fire counts 1.
//
// The same arm shape with once(in1), epochs in0=1; in1=5; in0=0; in0=1;
// in1=6; in1=7, gives [-1]; [0]; []; [-1]; [0]; [6]; []: the second
// activation of once emits twice (the first activation's 0, then 6).
// uniq(in1), epochs in0=1; in1=5; in0=0; in0=1; in1=5, gives [-1]; [0]; [5];
// [-1]; [5]; [5]: the woken uniq shows 5, then emits 5 again.
// take(#n: 1, ..), skip(#n: 1, ..) and hold(#clock, ..) show the same
// pre-restart value at the wake.
// schedule-v1: cap=64 events=512; in0=i64:1; in1=i64:5; in0=i64:2; in0=i64:1; in1=i64:6
{let v0 = select in0 {i64:0 => i64:-1, i64:1 => count(in1), _ => count(in1) + i64:100}; v0}
